# POST /proposal, the member's own void proposal uploaded again (R-1 of the DS re-review): carol's
# own Remove goes void after 24 h with nobody committing it, and she uploads the very same proposal
# again in the same epoch. It is HER proposal, so the instance re-arms it - live again, a fresh TTL -
# and answers as the first time; carol keeps it queued, alice's commit applies it, carol processes
# that commit, and she is out. (A 409 E_REMOVE_PENDING here would make carol withdraw her leave
# while nothing removes her.)
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0d0 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
sync carol
leave carol chat
advance_clock 25h
leave carol chat
commit alice chat
sync bob
sync carol
send alice chat carol has left
expect_decrypts bob chat carol has left
